this repository's own contents is in LICENSE.


1. What this repository contains
--------------------------------

All of the following is original work by the pikpik authors, licensed MIT
(see LICENSE):

    pc/                 the host port layer — Metal renderer, SDL2 window and
                        input, audio mixer and DSP emulation, memory-card
                        emulation, save sync, configuration, iOS entry point
    core-additions/     new source files added to the game tree by this port
    patches/            this port's modifications to the decompiled sources,
                        as unified diffs
    app/                the iOS Xcode shell project
    assets/icon.png     the application icon, generated by
                        assets/make_icon.py — an original drawing, not
                        traced, sampled, or derived from any other artwork
    tools/              development and diagnostic scripts
    docs/               documentation
    setup.sh, build_mac.sh, build_ios.sh, bundle_mac.sh


2. What this repository does NOT contain
----------------------------------------

    The Pikmin decompilation.  Not included. `setup.sh` fetches it at build
    time from its own upstream project (see section 3). Nothing under
    `patches/` is usable without it.

    Any game asset or data.  No textures, models, audio, video, text, level
    data, or executable code from the retail game is present in this
    repository in any form, compressed, encoded, or otherwise. A build is
    inert without a copy you supply yourself from your own disc.

    Not even a screenshot. The one in the README shows this port rendering
    Nintendo's artwork, so it is hosted outside this repository and embedded
    by URL. Cloning this repository copies no image of the game to your
    disk.

    Any tool for obtaining game data.  This repository contains no ripper,
    no downloader, and no circumvention code, and points at none.


